WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.005 --> 00:00:17.108
Cat meowed and hissed.

2
00:00:17.109 --> 00:00:21.517
She jumped at the swans.

3
00:00:21.518 --> 00:00:24.136
"What's she doing?" Tom said.

4
00:00:24.137 --> 00:00:26.604
"Those swans are mean!"

5
00:00:26.605 --> 00:00:29.447
The swans flew at Cat.

6
00:00:29.448 --> 00:00:31.489
They tried to bite her.

7
00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:35.338
Cat ran back toward the other carriages.

8
00:00:35.339 --> 00:00:41.240
The swans chased her.

9
00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:45.258
Walter waved his wand again and again.

10
00:00:45.259 --> 00:00:49.807
His king shouted loudly.

11
00:00:49.808 --> 00:00:52.870
The swans chased Cat.

12
00:00:52.871 --> 00:00:57.996
She jumped in front of the next carriage.

13
00:00:57.997 --> 00:01:03.370
Crash! Boom! All the carriages crashed into Walter's carriage.

14
00:01:03.371 --> 00:01:06.565
It was a royal mess.

15
00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:12.215
The kings yelled at each other.

16
00:01:12.216 --> 00:01:17.428
The wizards cast spells.

17
00:01:17.429 --> 00:01:21.584
Tom looked at his king. "Let's go, Your Majesty!"

18
00:01:21.585 --> 00:01:25.407
The king picked up the reins.

19
00:01:25.408 --> 00:01:32.334
He drove carefully around all the other carriages.

20
00:01:32.335 --> 00:01:37.904
Soon his carriage crossed the finish line.

21
00:01:37.905 --> 00:01:47.691
"I won!" the king shouted.

22
00:01:47.692 --> 00:01:51.693
"No fair!" grumbled the other kings.

23
00:01:51.694 --> 00:01:53.813
"My carriage is faster!"

24
00:01:53.814 --> 00:01:59.280
"No, mine is faster!"

25
00:01:59.281 --> 00:02:02.698
Cat jumped into Tom's pocket.

26
00:02:02.699 --> 00:02:05.852
"Are you hurt?" Tom asked.

27
00:02:05.853 --> 00:02:09.343
"Those swans are very mean!"

28
00:02:09.344 --> 00:02:11.396
Cat licked a paw.

29
00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:15.009
"The swans are very mean," she said.

30
00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:17.116
"But they are not very smart.

31
00:02:17.117 --> 00:02:23.746
It was easy to get away."

32
00:02:23.747 --> 00:02:26.386
"Good job, Tom," said May.

33
00:02:26.387 --> 00:02:31.057
Walter glared at Tom. "You were lucky this year.

34
00:02:31.058 --> 00:02:34.229
Next year my king will win!"

35
00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:42.484
Tom smiled. "We'll see about that!"
